nodecode-grok-acp is a rewrite of nicolasdmolina's nicolasdmolina/hermes-grok-acp:

https://github.com/nicolasdmolina/hermes-grok-acp
commit 2851d6667be7f1a9044fee5006a382699d942c6f
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Nicky Molina (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the provider a turn rides (the `grok' CLI on the user's own Grok
subscription, argv `agent --no-leader stdio'), the ACP session lifecycle
(initialize at protocol version 1, session/new, the model and the reasoning
effort as session config options, one session/prompt per round), the fold of
the streamed session/update text, the OpenAI-schema prompt with the
<tool_call> block contract and its parsing back into tool calls, the
fs/read_text_file and fs/write_text_file bridge, the permission answer, the
model and effort selection, the argument list the section names, and the
friendly note when the CLI is missing or logged out. Reimplemented in Common
Lisp against the Nodecode cell contract: one lane whose stream function
spawns the CLI and speaks the protocol, one hook answering the credential,
one listing the models.

Left out: the plugin's inheritance of its harness's ACP client, its
provider-profile and alias plumbing (`xai-grok-acp`, `grok-acp-agent`), the
`grok models` setup probe and its interactive `grok login`, the
provider-credential scrubbing of the child environment, the `GROK_HOME` and
`GROK_CLI_PATH`/`HERMES_GROK_ACP_ARGS` environment overrides (the section
names the same things), the error-text translation for a missing binary, and
the session-model-list fetch that only fed a picker. The plugin's whole
purpose, a Grok subscription answering turns keylessly through the CLI it is
already logged in to, is kept.
